Refactor this code by replacing %-style formatting with f-strings:

def greet(name):
    return 'Hello, %s! You have %d new messages.' % (name, count)

def path_msg(p):
    return 'File %s size=%s' % (p, os.path.getsize(p))

output:
def greet(name):
    return f'Hello, {name}! You have {count} new messages.'

def path_msg(p):
    return f'File {p} size={os.path.getsize(p)}'

What changed: %-formatting became f-strings; interpolation now happens where the expression lives, with editor support and no format-specifier mismatch risk.

