Refactor this code by replacing naive utcnow with timezone-aware datetimes:

def stamp():
    return datetime.utcnow().isoformat()

def is_expired(created):
    return datetime.utcnow() - created > timedelta(hours=24)

output:
from datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta

def stamp():
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()

def is_expired(created):
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc) - created > timedelta(hours=24)

What changed: datetime.utcnow() (deprecated, returns a naive datetime) became now(timezone.utc); timestamps are now offset-aware and compare safely.

