Refactor this code by using the modern struct-based or stdlib alternatives to hand-rolled utilities:

import json

def to_json(obj):
    s = json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, indent=2)
    return s + '\n'

def from_json(text):
    if text.endswith('\n'):
        text = text[:-1]
    return json.loads(text)

output:
import json

def to_json(obj):
    return json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, indent=2) + '\n'

def from_json(text):
    return json.loads(text.strip())

What changed: manual newline slicing became str.strip(); the helpers remain but no longer reimplement trimming with fragile index arithmetic.

